{
	"$comment": "Appearance and text overrides since SDK 1.2.0, grown in 2.0.0 (the card, text, muted and line colours, fontFamily, showBasketButton, showBasketBar, showAssistantName, showStarters, hideOrderHelp, hideVoice, hideCall, assistantName and five more labels) (ARCHITECTURE.md ADR-5.1, 5.4): what an app may change in the chat it opens. Canonical copy: packages/embed/fixtures/appearance_v1.json; every SDK keeps a byte-identical copy that its own tests read (scripts/check-sdk-fixtures.ts). `chatUrl` cases extend host_v1.json's: each appearance override is a search param of its own name (a flag is written `true` or `false`), and `expect` is compared as origin, path and an unordered set of decoded query pairs. `hostToPage` are the `appearance` messages setAppearance sends and the `text` messages setText sends: only the fields that were set. Text never goes on the URL.",
